### Figure 3 — as printed in the paper

Figure 3. Overview of our proposed method. In Stage 1, we cluster the dataset, and for each image within a cluster Ck, we reverse the ODE back to the noise space using a pretrained flow model to compute the new mean μ0,k and covariance Σ0,k for that cluster. In Stage 2, we apply optimal transport to finetune the pretrained flow model across all clusters, encouraging it to align with the distributional structure captured in Stage 1. During inference, we first sample a cluster index k, then draw a noise x from N(μ0,k, Σ0,k), and use this noise to generate an image through the finetuned flow model.

